a3 7. Nc2 a2 8. g3 Bf5 { The rest is relatively easy: sooner or later, Black's king will enter on either of the flanks, in similar fashion to Example 12 (Stoltz-Kashdan). } 9. Na1 Ke6 10. Nb3 Bg6 11. c4 ( { Abandoning the c-pawn; but after } 11. Ke3 Kd5 12. Kd2 Kc4 13. Na5 Kb5 14. Nb3 Ka4 15. Na1 Ka3 16. Kc1 h5 $1 { Black soon imposes a deadly zugzwang; e.g. } 17. c4 Bf5 18. c5 Be4 { - Baburin. } ) 
Bd3 12. Na1 ( { Or } 12. c5 Bc4 13. Na1 Kd5 { with similar play. } ) 
